     as the homepage search box, which spans the site column, "large, not
     smaller". 34rem was the old narrow panel. */
  .so-panel { position: relative; max-width: calc(var(--site-w) - 2 * var(--site-pad)); margin: 0 auto; }
  .so-panel .srch { max-width: none; }
  /* THE CLOSE BUTTON BELONGS TO THE PANEL (2026-08-06).
     It measured 28x32 and sat at top:-2.6rem, so on a 390px phone the only
     control that dismisses the overlay was a bare glyph floating 41px clear of
     the box it closes, on the blurred backdrop, at a size this project's own
     --tap-min forbids. Two faults, one cause: it was styled as a decoration
     rather than as a control.
     It is now a --tap-min square tab flush on the panel's top-right corner:
